        "thinking": "I'm trying to locate \"kram\" in the Uṇādi sūtras, checking whether it derives through the suffix \"tun,\" and searching for a relevant sūtra like \"क्रमितमिशतिस्तम्भामत इच्च\" that might account for forms like \"krimi.\"\n\nSince kram takes iṭ-āgama as a seṭ root, I'm working through whether \"krantu\" or similar arises through a general tun-suffix rule for valadi ārdhadhātuka cases.\n\nI'm trying to recall the exact uṇādi sutra involving kram and the tun suffix, questioning whether iṭ is added given the general rule that seṭ dhātus take iṭ before ārdhadhātuka suffixes starting with val, and searching for parallel examples like \"setu\" to confirm the pattern.\n\nLooking at other tun formations like tantu from tanu and jantu from jan — both seṭ roots that still form without iṭ, since uṇādi suffixes are often exceptions to the usual iṭ rule. By analogy, I conclude kram would similarly form krantu without iṭ, and there's no lengthening of the upadhā here since that dīrgha rule applies specifically to ktvā, not tun — so I'll settle on krantu as the answer.\n\n",
